 *
 * Hardware meaning is resolved by semantic/domain analysis.
 *
 * 12. distributed/AI/data
 *
 * The same lambda syntax remains reusable across these domains.
 *
 * ============================================================================
 * COMPLETION CRITERIA
 * ============================================================================
 *
 * This file is DONE when:
 *
 *     [x] It is a parser grammar.
 *     [x] It uses tokenVocab = ZamaniLexer.
 *     [x] It defines exactly one public lambdaExpression rule.
 *     [x] It defines no lexer rules.
 *     [x] It does not define parameterList.
 *     [x] It does not define typeExpression.
 *     [x] It does not define expression.
 *     [x] It does not define blockExpression.
 *     [x] It does not define closure capture syntax.
 *     [x] It does not define function declarations.
 *     [x] It does not define function types.
 *     [x] It has no hardware-specific syntax.
 *     [x] It has no quantum-specific syntax.
 *     [x] It has no fixed resource capacity.
 *     [x] It has no machine-size constants.
 *     [x] It has no semantic actions.
 *     [x] It has no predicates.
 *     [x] It has no embedded Rust.
 *     [x] It requires no unsafe Rust.
 *     [x] It supports zero parameters.
 *     [x] It supports source-defined arbitrary parameter counts.
 *     [x] It supports typed parameters.
 *     [x] It supports parameter defaults through parameterList.
 *     [x] It supports optional explicit return types.
 *     [x] It supports expression bodies.
 *     [x] It supports block bodies.
